                "submission_id": "submission:correctness-review:1:2d61c324",
                "summary": "Three defects in the continuous view. (1) recognise.ts:436-441: when a too-long movement is dropped on its last hand frame (the hands leave right then), the buffer is emptied and own.dropping stays true, so the next real gesture is silently discarded as the 'rest' (reproduced: 102 frames held up, hands down, then a 10-frame gesture gives analysed=[], taken=[]; with 103 frames it gives [10]). Fix: keep the triggering frame (usedTo = frames.length - 2) or clear dropping once the hands are away for longer than SEGMENT_GAP_MS. (2) recognise.ts:972 still clears previewSlot for 'listening', so each redraw (tile taken, dropped line) takes the preview and 'Bild an / aus' out and back in; a focused picture toggle drops focus to the page (Chromium: a removed and re-added focused button leaves activeElement=BODY), and the draw does not count it as lost (pictureShown is true). This breaks NG-48 and the NG-47 place() intent. Fix: add state.kind !== 'listening' to that condition. (3) recognise.ts:630-633 with 1018: the tiles are shown newest first, so each take moves every older tile one place; sayWord checks only the taken concept's own takenAt and not aimed(pressAt), so a press aimed at an old tile within RECOGNISE_GUARD_MS of the redraw says the word of the tile that moved into its place. Fix: also require aimed(pressAt) in sayWord, or append tiles newest last. Correct as checked: the index map (segments are slices of the same sided objects); the usedTo branches; the bounded buffer; force with Infinity; the takenAt reset on a repeat; confirm and leave; switchCamera and onSeen; sw.js precache; the evaluation fixes; the docs table matches a rerun (away 600/699/1000; rest 2000/3000; away over rests). The tests fail without the change. 70/70 node tests pass.",
